\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.17}{\ignorespaces This figure shows the fit plasma parameters from the single ended TREX cells on the left and the differential D-TACQ digitizers on the right. The differential digitizers have a much higher sampling rate letting us better resolve the plasma dynamics and the error bars are far smaller. It can be seen that the fitting routine sometimes has erroneous fits as can be seen in the right panel at around $t = 0.018088$ s.}}{85}{figure.caption.122}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multitip_trex_vs_dtacq}{{3.17}{85}{This figure shows the fit plasma parameters from the single ended TREX cells on the left and the differential D-TACQ digitizers on the right. The differential digitizers have a much higher sampling rate letting us better resolve the plasma dynamics and the error bars are far smaller. It can be seen that the fitting routine sometimes has erroneous fits as can be seen in the right panel at around $t = 0.018088$ s}{figure.caption.122}{}}
